minecraft takes a stand on nfts discord  and xbox team up and more  minecraft developer mo yang is making it  clear that it will not allow blockchain  technology like nfts to be integrated  within its massively popular game  stating it believes nfts to be quote  inconsistent with the long-term joy and  success of our players nfts or  non-fungible tokens are digital assets  on the blockchain like jpegs of artwork  or even in-game files that one purchase  grant ownership of that particular file  however those files can be and often are  copied or stolen calling into question  exactly how valuable these digital files  truly are as mo yang explains in a new  blog post allowing server owners to  implement nft integration and play to  earn features which could reward players  with nft forms of in-game skins and  items would take the quote focus away  from playing the game and allow for  profiteering the crux of the matter  comes down to the fact that allowing  players to earn nft rewards would create  an ecosystem of haves and have-nots  which goes against minecraft's values of  inclusion and playing together  in other news xbox is finally  introducing built-in discord support  today select xbox insiders will be able  to try out the integration while  everyone else will have to wait for the  support to expand in the coming weeks  this new feature seems to only support  voice chat and not discord's text-based  communication there is also no dedicated  app on xbox yet so make sure you have  your mobile device ready because you'll  need it to transfer audio over to the  console using the new join on xbox  button once you're in a call that's been  transferred over you'll be able to see  who's on the call with you and who's  speaking the same as if you were on  discord on mobile or pc you'll also be  able to adjust sound as well as switch  between discord voice and xbox game chat  last year playstation invested in  discord but it was only a minority  investment the chat service seems to  have no interest in being acquired at  this point in time as a report  circulated last year that microsoft had  considered acquiring discord for around  10 billion dollars though the latter did  not go through with it switching gears  to diablo immortal following a new  update players will be able to convert  their current character into a new class  every 7 days at no cost the swap can be  made at the new shifting flames brazier  in west march and players will have the  option of immediately reverting back to  the character's previous class should  they decide they made a mistake blizzard  states that it will not allow players to  purchase the ability to change classes  more frequently characters that undergo  a class change will have placeholder  gear with an equivalent rank to the gear  equipped by the player prior to the  class change and gear equipped by the  previous version of the character will  be placed in the player's inventory man  i really convinced myself that i was  gonna play diablo immortal a decent  amount when it first released i'm  nowhere close to the controversial end  game let me know if you're still playing  it and what you think of today's nft  minecraft news as well as the discord  xbox news and i'll see you tomorrow
 

